From 94953d948e46e04ae2f286c991c387d6fd624c4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:19:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPUOP-1131: Implement smi-power thread, POWER seqlock record
 and shutdown/join

Run the POWER tier on its own internal thread so the 1 s FAST sweep and the
slow violation_status read cannot stall it (GPUOP-1122 design rev 3,
power-thread-and-tiers / amdsmi-watcher).

- core: AGA_THREAD_ID_WATCHER_POWER after AGA_THREAD_ID_WATCHER.
- smi_watch: smi-power thread (sdk::lib::thread, CONTROL role, no event
  loop). Active only while FastPeriodMs < 1000 and the power view has a
  watch, else parked on sem_timedwait(100 ms). While active: one
  smi_watch_power_read() per needed GPU per tick (POWER fields reset to NA,
  filled on success), absolute deadlines with clock_nanosleep(TIMER_ABSTIME,
  EINTR retry), overruns counted as (now - next) / p + 1 with no catch-up
  burst, rate-limited WARN. No allocation, task, proto or Write per tick.
- Per-GPU seqlock record g_power_rec (atomic seq + atomic values); the
  writer never waits; readers retry up to 64 times (yielding after 8),
  then use the copy with a VERBOSE trace.
- Ownership hand-over: g_power_active makes smi_watch_tick_plan() report
  power_by_watcher = false; the amdsmi sweep then takes POWER from
  smi_watch_power_snapshot(). The snapshot returns bool per GPU, so a GPU
  the power thread does not sample is still read by the sweep.
- Power view (immutable shared_ptr) rebuilt by smi-watcher on subscribe and
  inactive-subscriber cleanup; smi_watch_set_periods and view publishes
  post the wake semaphore.
- amdsmi: smi_watch_power_read = one amdsmi_get_gpu_metrics_info +
  smi_watch_fill_power_fields. Thread started after watcher_init();
  teardown stops/joins it first, then smi-watcher, then amdsmi_shut_down.
  Stop never uses pthread_cancel. The period check accepts sub-second
  periods (cache rule kept), OP_NOT_SUPPORTED only if the thread failed
  to start.
- mock: period check accepts sub-second periods; synthetic
  smi_watch_power_read (the mock watcher/thread start is GPUOP-1133).
- GPUWatch status MissedTicks = smi_watch_missed_ticks().

GIM/WSL unchanged (sub-second still OP_NOT_SUPPORTED). Partial frames and
subscriber queues are GPUOP-1132. Build and mock verification run in the
exporter CI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
